# Quality Standards Rules
# Loaded when quality standards are required
# Auto-generated by Dynamic Cursor Rules System

## QUALITY STANDARDS (NON-NEGOTIABLE)

### Zero Hallucinations
- If uncertain → Research or ask, NEVER guess
- If can't verify → Document uncertainty
- If below confidence → Pivot, don't force
- Always validate information before using
- Document sources and confidence levels

### Test-Driven Development
- Write tests for ALL code
- Aim for 100% pass rate
- Run tests after every change
- Fix failures immediately
- No code without tests

### Perfect Alignment
- Every task traces to north star (goals/GOAL_TREE.yaml)
- Check alignment hourly
- If drifting → Realign immediately
- Cosmetic work = forbidden
- Document goal alignment for each task

### Code Quality Standards
- Clean, readable, maintainable code
- Type hints everywhere
- Comprehensive docstrings
- Production-quality always
- Follow established patterns

### Documentation Standards
- Document everything comprehensively
- Use clear, concise language
- Include examples and use cases
- Keep documentation up-to-date
- Version control all documentation

### Performance Standards
- Optimize for performance
- Profile before optimizing
- Measure improvements
- Document performance metrics
- Monitor resource usage

### Security Standards
- Follow security best practices
- Validate all inputs
- Handle errors gracefully
- Use secure coding patterns
- Regular security reviews

### Error Handling
- Comprehensive error handling
- Graceful degradation
- Clear error messages
- Log errors appropriately
- Recovery mechanisms

### Code Review Standards
- All code must be reviewed
- Check for quality issues
- Verify test coverage
- Ensure documentation
- Validate alignment

### Continuous Improvement
- Learn from mistakes
- Update processes
- Share knowledge
- Regular retrospectives
- Measure and improve

---
